  <!-- 3. 24-48H DELTA -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>On 27 August 2026, CENTCOM chief Admiral Brad Cooper announced that US forces had cleared Iranian sea mines from the Strait of Hormuz transit routes, using Navy divers, Navy SEALs, and multi-service air assets deployed over several months of quiet operations. Lloyd's List recorded 114 commercial transits between 17 and 27 August — an average of 11.4 per day, roughly 12% of pre-war norms — while US allies privately assessed that mines may remain outside the formally cleared corridors, and shipping insurers had not reinstated Hormuz war-risk cover as of 30 August. → moved <span class="cite">F4</span>, <span class="cite">F5</span></p>
      <p>Qatar's Prime Minister Sheikh Mohammed bin Abdulrahman Al Thani arrived in Tehran on 28–30 August, the third senior mediator in four days, meeting with President Pezeshkian, Foreign Minister Araghchi, and SNSC Secretary Rezaei. Rezaei stated in an Al Manar interview on 28 August that Iran was "preparing a list of conditions" for Hormuz reopening at mediators' request; per Axios reporting from 5 August, Araghchi had agreed "in principle" to a Hormuz deal framework during the preceding weekend, pending Mojtaba Khamenei's approval, which remained unconfirmed as of 30 August. → moved <span class="cite">F1</span>, <span class="cite">F2</span></p>
      <p>Iran's Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei issued a written message to Gulf Arab rulers on 30 August, urging them to confront what he described as the "real enemy," per the Times of Israel liveblog — a framing that did not name the United States or Israel directly but departed from the conciliatory register of recent state-media coverage. Concurrently, USS Abraham Lincoln passed Singapore on 30 August, heading home after a record 250-plus-day deployment in support of the regional campaign. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span></p>
      <p>The United States imposed new sanctions on Hezbollah on 20 August and issued fresh warnings of economic pressure on Iran, which the Iranian government acknowledged by reiterating that "diplomacy and defense are complementary and coordinated tools." An acute fuel shortage deepened across Iran through late August, with motorists reporting hours-long queues and dry stations as of 26 August, while senior officials discussed domestic price reform with unusual candor for wartime state-media coverage. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>Israeli settlers attacked a Palestinian woman and an NBC News crew in the West Bank on 29 August, per the Times of Israel liveblog — drawing renewed international attention to conditions on the ground with Israel's October 27 election two months away. Haaretz analysis published 28 August described Netanyahu's bloc as "stuck" in polls, with neither bloc reaching the 61-seat majority needed to govern following an election that has so far defied projection. → supports <span class="cite">F7</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. SCENARIO MAP -->
  <div class="section" id="scenario-map">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Scenario Map
      <span class="meta">Computed from Forecast Board · 1 sentence per scenario</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="scenario-map">
      <div class="prob-bar-container">
        <div class="prob-bar prob-escalation" style="width:25%;">Escalation 25%</div>
