        <span class="p">15–25%</span>
        <div class="drivers">Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei was killed in the Feb 28 strikes; Mojtaba Khamenei assumed the role. The IRGC remains organizationally coherent. The acute fuel crisis and sanctions pressure create domestic instability, but no credible armed opposition has emerged to threaten central authority. Regime cohesion under wartime conditions has historically been reinforced, not undermined, by external pressure in the Iranian case.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="regime-row">
        <span class="name">🇮🇱 Israel (Netanyahu not PM by end of 2026)</span>
        <span class="p">55–65%</span>
        <div class="drivers">Knesset dissolved July 17; election Oct 27. Polls consistently show Netanyahu's bloc at 49-52 seats, below the 61 needed. Eisenkot's Yashar polling 21-25 seats. Neither bloc has a clear path to majority. There is a 55-65% probability Netanyahu does not lead the next government — reflecting both polling reality and the difficulty of coalition arithmetic. The probability range for Netanyahu remaining PM is therefore 35-45%.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
